# Cursor Rules for AI Video Generator Project

## Prompt Generation Rules

### NEVER Reference Existing Media
- ❌ NEVER mention movie titles (Spider-Verse, Matrix, Blade Runner, etc.)
- ❌ NEVER mention character names (Spider-Man, Neo, etc.)
- ❌ NEVER mention franchise names (Marvel, DC, Star Wars, etc.)
- ❌ NEVER use "X-inspired" or "X-style" referencing media

### Instead: Describe Visual Style Directly
- ✅ Use technical art terms: "hybrid 2D/3D animation", "cel-shaded", "comic book aesthetics"
- ✅ Describe specific visual effects: "bold dynamic outlines", "halftone patterns", "chromatic aberration"
- ✅ Describe animation techniques: "varied frame timing", "motion blur trails", "speed lines"

## Image Generation Prompts

### Style Keywords to Use
- Animation: hybrid 2D/3D, hand-drawn details, cel-shaded, painterly brush strokes
- Visual Effects: Ben-Day dots, halftone patterns, chromatic aberration, motion blur, speed lines
- Aesthetic: bold dynamic outlines, varying line weights, imperfect hand-drawn edges, intentional imperfections
- Post-processing: film grain texture, pop art influences, high contrast vibrant colors

### NEVER Include
- Movie/show references
- Character costume descriptions from media
- Franchise-specific terminology

## Setting: Slavic Steampunk Post-Apocalyptic

### Core Elements
- **Slavic:** Traditional patterns, folk motifs, Orthodox architecture elements, Cyrillic aesthetics
- **Steampunk:** Brass mechanisms, copper pipes, steam vents, clockwork, Victorian-era tech, coal-powered
- **Post-Apocalyptic:** Ruins, weathered surfaces, nature reclaiming technology, makeshift repairs

### Visual Vocabulary
- Materials: brass, copper, bronze, worn leather, aged wood, tarnished metal
- Tech: clockwork mechanisms, steam-powered, gear-driven, pneumatic systems, analog dials
- Architecture: Orthodox onion domes with brass plating, steam-pipe spires, mechanical bell towers
- Energy: steam clouds, pressure valves releasing, coal ember glow, mechanical sparks
- Clothing: Victorian-era base with Slavic embroidery, brass goggles, leather straps, gear accessories

## Testing & Development
- Use `uv` for all Python operations
- Never disable git hooks or use `--no-verify`
- Write tests before fixing defects
- Maintain 80%+ test coverage
